<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ninh Bình Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ninh Bình is a province in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, on the southern edge of the Red River delta, with its capital at the city of Ninh Bình. It contains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-lu">Hoa Lư</a>, the capital of the Đinh and Early Lê dynasties in the 10th century, and the limestone karst landscape of Tràng An, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> since 2014. In 2025 it was enlarged by merger with Hà Nam and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nam-dinh">Nam Định</a> provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ninh-binh-province.jpg" alt="Ninh Bình Province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tuan Mai · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tam_Coc_by_Tuan_Mai_%22007%22_(8888350545).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
